cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  wavelab reproduces the branching Monte Carlo method of Chan and Privault.
  If you use this code, please cite the paper (preferred-citation) as well as
  this repository.
title: "wavelab: a solver toolbox for nonlinear wave equations"
abstract: >-
  Finite-difference and branching Monte Carlo solvers for nonlinear wave
  equations u_tt - c^2 Laplacian(u) = sum a_k u^k with complex wave speed and
  complex data, in space dimensions 1, 2 and 3. Built to reproduce and study the
  ill-posed (c = i) elliptic Cauchy problems of Chan and Privault (2026).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Liao
    given-names: Tianrui
    alias: RichardMilos233
    email: richardmilos233@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Nanyang Technological University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RichardMilos233/wavelab"
keywords:
  - nonlinear wave equations
  - branching processes
  - Monte Carlo method
  - ill-posed problems
  - finite differences

# The method this toolbox implements and studies.
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: >-
    Probabilistic representation and classical solutions of wave equations with
    complex polynomial nonlinearities
  authors:
    - family-names: Chan
      given-names: "Joshua J. Y."
      affiliation: >-
        School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological
        University, Singapore
      email: joshuaju001@e.ntu.edu.sg
    - family-names: Privault
      given-names: Nicolas
      affiliation: >-
        School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological
        University, Singapore
      email: nprivault@ntu.edu.sg
  year: 2026
  month: 1
  notes: "Manuscript dated 28 January 2026."
